WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:18.676
Unit fourteen: Part 5: Business Vocabulary and Collocations. Today you will choose the word that collocates naturally in workplace sentences.

4
00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:21.698
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:26.052
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:27.953
Collocation.

7
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.635
Collocation means words that often go together.

8
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.400
Make a decision is a collocation.

9
00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:37.506
Your turn. Say: Collocation.

10
00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.472
Collocation.

11
00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:43.264
Reduce.

12
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.110
Reduce means to make smaller.

13
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.182
Reduce costs.

14
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:51.645
Your turn. Say: Reduce.

15
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.548
Reduce.

16
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:57.226
Submit.

17
00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:00.205
Submit means to give for approval.

18
00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:02.201
Submit the report.

19
00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:05.156
Your turn. Say: Submit.

20
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.001
Submit.

21
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.670
Attend.

22
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:13.660
Attend means to be present at.

23
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.448
Attend a meeting.

24
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.969
Your turn. Say: Attend.

25
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:22.753
Attend.

26
00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:24.274
Reach.

27
00:01:25.283 --> 00:01:27.051
Reach means to get to a goal.

28
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.965
Reach an agreement.

29
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.376
Your turn. Say: Reach.

30
00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:36.037
Reach.

31
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:37.866
Place an order.

32
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.964
Place an order means to ask a company to supply goods.

33
00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.992
Place an order online.

34
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:47.456
Your turn. Say: Place an order.

35
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.406
Place an order.

36
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.441
Meet a deadline.

37
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.693
Meet a deadline means to finish on time.

38
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.888
We must meet the deadline.

39
00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:02.356
Your turn. Say: Meet a deadline.

40
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.526
Meet a deadline.

41
00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:08.737
Take responsibility.

42
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.887
Take responsibility means to accept duty for something.

43
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:15.785
He takes responsibility for sales.

44
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:19.663
Your turn. Say: Take responsibility.

45
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.058
Take responsibility.

46
00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:28.959
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:32.548
Visal, which words appear a lot in Part 5?

48
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:45.114
Business verbs like submit, attend, reduce and reach, and nouns like budget, schedule, policy and invoice. You often need to know which word goes with which.

49
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:48.054
How do I learn collocations?

50
00:02:49.150 --> 00:03:02.623
Learn short phrases instead of single words: submit a report, reach an agreement, meet a deadline and place an order. Say them aloud until they sound natural.

51
00:03:03.717 --> 00:03:05.229
What mistakes happen?

52
00:03:06.317 --> 00:03:16.490
Students choose a word that has a good meaning but the wrong partner, such as do an agreement instead of reach an agreement, or make a deadline instead of meet a deadline.

53
00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:19.331
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.183 --> 00:03:25.016
Grammar focus: Strategy: learn phrases, not single words.

55
00:03:25.316 --> 00:03:26.584
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.283 --> 00:03:29.376
We must meet the deadline on Friday.

57
00:03:30.283 --> 00:03:32.887
The two companies reached an agreement last week.

58
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:41.699
Learn business collocations as whole phrases. When two options look possible, choose the one that sounds natural with the words nearby.

59
00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.811
Be careful! Don't say: I say 'do an agreement'.

60
00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:50.428
Say: I say 'reach an agreement'.

61
00:03:50.728 --> 00:03:52.321
Learn collocations.

62
00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.704
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.919
Business Phrases.

64
00:03:58.219 --> 00:04:01.113
Piseth keeps a list of business collocations.

65
00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.680
He writes submit a report and reach an agreement.

66
00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:08.572
He also writes place an order and meet a deadline.

67
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.891
On the test he sees the gap: reach an ___.

68
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.840
He chooses agreement because he remembers the phrase.

69
00:04:16.933 --> 00:04:21.132
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:21.983 --> 00:04:23.727
A collocation is blank.

71
00:04:24.027 --> 00:04:28.412
A, a spelling. B, a number. C, words that go together.

72
00:04:31.967 --> 00:04:35.208
The answer is C: words that go together.

73
00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.560
Which is natural?

74
00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:42.674
A, reach an agreement. B, do an agreement. C, take an agreement.

75
00:04:46.233 --> 00:04:48.604
The answer is A: reach an agreement.

76
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.517
We must blank the deadline.

77
00:04:51.817 --> 00:04:54.623
A, do. B, meet. C, make.

78
00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.189
The answer is B: meet.

79
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.850
You blank a report.

80
00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.421
A, drink. B, grow. C, submit.

81
00:05:09.967 --> 00:05:12.140
The answer is C: submit.

82
00:05:13.283 --> 00:05:14.737
What does Piseth keep?

83
00:05:15.037 --> 00:05:19.585
A, a list of phrases. B, a diary of films. C, a map.

84
00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.504
The answer is A: a list of phrases.

85
00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.886
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.168
How do you learn business collocations?

87
00:05:41.983 --> 00:05:43.542
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:43.842 --> 00:05:57.364
I learn them as short phrases, such as reach an agreement and meet a deadline. I write them in a list with an example, and I say them aloud. In the test I choose the word that sounds natural with the words around it.

89
00:05:57.664 --> 00:05:59.373
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:00.283 --> 00:06:06.372
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: learn phrases, not single words.

91
00:06:06.672 --> 00:06:11.054
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

92
00:06:11.354 --> 00:06:13.728
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:14.028 --> 00:06:17.331
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

